{
  "startedAt": "2026-10-12T08:25:11.996Z",
  "steps": [
    "Actual seventeen-module/thirty-three-capability HTTP editor mounts independent bulk copy. Source selections are empty, offset XYZ is zero and no identities are allocated until explicit selection. A three-source scene displays 125 remaining object slots but only three possible copies this time. Native BOM/CRLF/escaped-key source and literal author names are shown; readonly preview records actual software-WebGL pixels.",
    "Explicit reverse-click selection canonicalizes append order to source declarations, including hidden sources. Zero offset produces real structural copies with fresh UUIDs, original names without suffix and unchanged geometry. Complete originals and all other scene fields/BOM/CRLF remain. Rechecking, deselect/reselect, query and Chinese/English/Japanese 390px preserve allocated mapping and approval. Cancel changes neither memory nor disk.",
    "Closing/reopening starts a fresh allocation map. A common XYZ offset affects only appended copies, leaving every original unchanged. Apply accepts the exact advanced owner receipt and updates source memory only. Fresh software-GPU preview reflects the new geometry. Ordinary Save writes exact reviewed bytes; reopening reads five persisted objects and fresh IDs for another explicit selection.",
    "64 selected originals plus 64 appended copies are the maximum successful batch and exactly fill 128 objects, including hidden sources, with unique mapped identities and unchanged originals. 128 originals show zero slots and cannot approve copy. Selecting all 65 originals exceeds its 63-slot budget and is explicitly blocked without truncating selection. If only one candidate copy exceeds final position bounds, the native operation rejects the whole batch while preserving mapping and raw offset.",
    "Silent checkbox, offset, query, mapping dataset or displayed new UUID mutation revokes approval. Source edits with or without input cannot be overwritten by an older copy candidate. Old closed-session and old-query rows cannot allocate IDs or change a new selection; current rows still work. No invalid attempt applies or saves.",
    "Actual portable modules retain the eighth private authoring brand. Serialized clones and cross-domain distribution application reject copy proposals. Reusing an existing identity is rejected at bridge semantic identity admission with scene3d_copy_invalid. Zero offset remains a valid structural proposal. The pure proof has no writer or Save port.",
    "A valid appended-copy draft still uses ordinary editor Save preconditions. External disk change opens the existing conflict dialog; Cancel retains external bytes and the unsaved reviewed candidate independently. Copy never implicitly saves or writes metadata.",
    "WebGL2-unavailable injection affects drawing only. Native structural copy review remains available with all sixteen assembled modules, without renderer, World, backend or implicit Save authority."
  ],
